<title>USA: J.C. Penney Q4 oper shr $1.20 vs $1.31.</title>
<headline>J.C. Penney Q4 oper shr $1.20 vs $1.31.</headline>
<dateline>PLANO, Texas 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr primary     $0.36		    $1.31</p>
<p> Oper shr	  $1.20		    $1.31</p>
<p> Net		 94			 326</p>
<p> Revs		8,157		    6,632</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary231.8		    227.0</p>
<p>	  12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr primary     $2.25		    $3.33</p>
<p> Oper shr	  $3.17		    $3.33</p>
<p> Net		 565			838</p>
<p> Revs		22,653		   20,562</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary229.1		    228.7</p>
<p>(All data above in millions, except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said in Q4 1996 it incurred one-time charges of $0.84 per share, primarily related to the integration of drug store acquisitions, including the closing of drug stores and certain support functions, and the write-down of certain assets. Full company name is J.C. Penney Co Inc.</p>
